BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-194582@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260713T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T210000
SUMMARY:Boston’s Exclusive First-Look Screening of "The Odyssey"
LOCATION:Offsite: AMC Boston Common
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are on 
 Waitlist\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194582\n\n6:3
 0PM Doors Open\, 7:00PM-10:00PM Screening\nBe among the first to experienc
 e one of the year's most anticipated cinematic events with a first look sc
 reening of Christopher Nolan's highly anticipated adaptation of The Odysse
 y.\n\nThis summer\, defy the gods. Universal Pictures proudly presents the
  new film by Christopher Nolan. A sweeping mythological epic inspired by H
 omer's timeless poem\, The Odyssey\, staring Matt Damon\, Tom Holland\, 
 Anne Hathaway\, Robert Pattison\, Lupita Nyong'o\, Zendaya and\, Charlize 
 Theron. The film follows Odysseus\, the legendary King of Ithaca perilous 
 decade- long journey home after the Trojan War as he confronts mythical cr
 eatures\, vengeful gods\, and extraordinary trials in a relentless quest t
 o reunite with his wife\, Penelope.\n\nJoin us for an unforgettable evenin
 g of epic storytelling\, breathtaking spectacle\, and one of the year's mo
 st anticipated cinematic experiences.\n\n*This event is complimentary and 
 reserved for members only. Please note that the screening will begin promp
 tly at 7:00PM with no trailers preceding the film.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194582
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191168@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260714T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260714T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260714T190000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Man Made" with Karen Korellis Reuther
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unlimit
 ed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191168\n\n5:00PM Re
 ception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nWhat if the world around us was not designed 
 with everyone in mind?\n\nJoin us for an illuminating conversation with Ka
 ren Korellis Reuther - designer\, educator\, inclusion advocate\, and auth
 or for an exclusive first look of the forthcoming book MAN-MADE: How We D
 esigned a World That Leaves Women Out\, and How We Can Make It Right. Draw
 ing on more than four decades of experience\, including leadership roles a
 t Nike and Reebok and her current work at Harvard's Graduate School of Des
 ign\, Karen explores the hidden ways gender bias has been built into the p
 roducts\, systems\, and spaces we encounter every day.\n\nFrom personal pr
 otective equipment and athletic footwear to healthcare\, transportation\, 
 and public infrastructure\, MAN-MADE reveals how design decisions rooted
  in a male default continue to shape women's experiences\, often with prof
 ound consequences. Through compelling research\, real-world examples\, and
  a forward-looking vision for change\, Karen invites us to reconsider the 
 world we have inherited - and imagine one designed for everyone.\n\n*This 
 event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Light bites and refr
 eshments will be served. A pre-release of the book will be available for p
 urchase at this event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191168
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-194581@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260715T133000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T150000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Gallery by Denise Matejic 
LOCATION:The Terrace
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194581\n\n1:30PM Reception\, 2
 :00PM Discussion\nPlease join The 'Quin House art curator\, Kate Chertavia
 n for a discussion together with The ‘Quin House Co-Founder Sandy Edgerl
 ey on the works of her mother\, artist Denise Matejic. On view in the Terr
 ace through July 23rd\, the pop-up exhibition features 21 artworks in a va
 riety of media created throughout her career. Inspired by the rural landsc
 apes and cityscapes of Western Europe where she grew up\, as well as the s
 uburban landscape here in New England and beyond\, her work is a celebrati
 on of the beauty found in the world around us. Together\, Kate and Sandy w
 ill explore Denise's artistic practice and how it has inspired Sandy's lif
 elong love of art. Members will enjoy this afternoon experience over tea a
 nd light bites.  \n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for membe
 rs only.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194581
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191172@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260715T200000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T223000
SUMMARY:Sail Boston: Luxury Yacht Valiant
LOCATION:Offsite: Rowes Wharf Gate C
DESCRIPTION:Category: Member Mixer\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Waitlis
 t Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191172\n\nAs Bo
 ston welcomes a once-in-a-generation gathering of the world's most magnifi
 cent tall ships in celebration of America's 250th anniversary\, join fello
 w members aboard luxury yacht Valiant for an unforgettable evening on the 
 harbor.\n\nDeparting from Rowes Wharf\, this exclusive cruise offers a fro
 nt-row vantage point to Sail Boston 2026\, as an international fleet of hi
 storic tall ships and military vessels fills the harbor in a remarkable di
 splay of maritime tradition and global camaraderie. As dusk settles over t
 he city\, enjoy unparalleled views of the fleet before the evening culmina
 tes with a spectacular fireworks display illuminating the Boston skyline.\
 n\nThroughout the cruise\, guests will enjoy an open bar and a selection o
 f elevated bites while taking in one of the most anticipated events of the
  Semiquincentennial celebration from the best seat in the harbor.\n\n*This
  event is offered at $295 per person and is reserved for members\, plus 
 one registered guest age 21+. Complimentary light bites and refreshments w
 ill be served. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served.
  Please note that this event will take place rain or shine. Valiant is par
 tially covered\, and in the event of rough water conditions\, the vessel w
 ill remain docked. Members will meet at Rowes Wharf Gate C\, located direc
 tly in front of the Boston Harbor Hotel. Parking is available at the Bost
 on Harbor Hotel.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191172
CATEGORIES:Member Mixer
END:VEVENT
